.TH dirname 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
dirname \- strip the last component from a path
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dirname
.I name
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dirname
prints
.I name
with its last component removed, or a single dot if
.I name
has no slash in it.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# dirname /usr/man/man1/ls.1
/usr/man/man1
.fi
.SH NOTES
With no argument, or with more than one,
.B dirname
prints nothing and exits 0.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR basename (1)
